  "description": "Editorial recognizability tiers for a general EN/ES audience. 1 = unmistakable (shape, flag, capital and location are common knowledge), 2 = household name with less automatic geography, 3 = known name but vague geography, 4 = specialist/quiz knowledge. Population is deliberately not a factor; these tiers replace the old World Bank population quartiles as the per-round difficulty default. shapeHolds lists countries whose territory is scattered atolls: they stay playable in flag, capital and map rounds but are excluded from the silhouette round.",
